<title>CHINA: China Jan-Nov trade surplus $14 billion - radio.</title>
<headline>China Jan-Nov trade surplus $14 billion - radio.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China registered a trade surplus of about $14.0 billion in the first 11 months of 1996, state radio said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The radio gave January to November exports as $132.78 billion, up 0.9 percent from the year-ago period and imports as $118.81 billion, up 4.5 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>China registered a trade surplus of $12.01 in the first 10 months and $3.91 billion in October alone.</p>
</text>
